/* spy_targets.c -- per-model addresses for the additive pedals' patches (core/spy_patch.c).
 *
 * GENERATED by the derivation tools, do not edit by hand. Pedalboard: the hand-made analysis, confirmed on hardware.
 * MX5 / Gigboard: derived from it by matching every Pedalboard site in that model's stock 2.7 Evil (masked instruction
 * windows around an anchor map of 8M unique 16-word windows, then a structural check per site: same instruction,
 * same call target, same table contents, same reader count). EXPERIMENTAL: never run on a device. Differences found:
 *  - descriptor table P3 and the one function that reads it (with its names+16 literal and its `cmp #0xa8`) do not
 *    exist on MX5 / Gigboard, so there is nothing to relocate or bump for it;
 *  - several functions are compiled differently (registers, struct offsets): every site still holds the same
 *    instruction and immediate, only the registers differ, and the expected word is the model's own;
 *  - hook D (the picker retrying ids 3 and 4 when a pedal's first two are in use) is not ported: picker_exit = 0,
 *    the stock picker behaviour is kept and 4-instance pedals are refused.
 * Every value here is checked against the stock binary at patch time (expected old words), so a wrong model or
 * firmware build refuses instead of producing a bad image. */
